Stage 2 — Finish chr22 prototype

This stage is not publishable. Its job is to prove the machinery works.

2.1 Separate PCA dataset from scoring dataset

You already made a PCA/QC file. Now make a scorebase file without global MAF filtering.

 Keep this for PCA:
plink2 --pfile chr22 `
  --geno 0.02 `
  --mind 0.02 `
  --maf 0.01 `
  --make-pgen `
  --out chr22.qc
 Create this for scoring:
plink2 --pfile chr22 `
  --geno 0.02 `
  --mind 0.02 `
  --make-pgen `
  --out chr22.scorebase

Reason: MAF filtering is good for PCA but can remove real PGS variants.

2.2 Assign robust variant IDs
 Use allele-explicit IDs.
plink2 --pfile chr22.scorebase `
  --set-all-var-ids '@:#:$r:$a' `
  --make-pgen `
  --out chr22.scorebase.id
 Confirm .pvar IDs look like:
22:16050075:A:G
