20.1 Introduction
 PRS portability is a major barrier.
 Accuracy decay cannot be reduced to global ancestry distance.
 Score distribution shift is not the same as prediction portability.
 Open datasets lack phenotypes but can measure mechanisms.
 Cross-ancestry GWAS concordance gives phenotype-free validation.
 FAIRGEN-Open predicts and decomposes portability risk.
